#!/bin/sh
# CodeHydra background wrapper.
#
# Runs the given command transparently (same stdio, same exit code). Its only
# job is to put the "ch-bg" marker into the command string CodeHydra sees in the
# agent's background task list, so this background shell is excluded from keeping
# the workspace busy. Wrap long-lived background processes with it:
#   ch-bg npm run dev
#
# `ch bg` does the same thing and is the canonical spelling. This one stays a
# self-contained passthrough rather than a shim: it must work with no
# dependencies at all — before `ch` has been rendered, and without an
# interpreter — and its whole implementation is the line below.
exec "$@"
